# How role descriptions are written (the long description in Match Info and /r is built from these parts)
#   <Role>.Blurb        One line shown in the intro
#   <Role>.Summary      One sentence: "A <team> who can ..."
#   <Role>.WinCond      Only when the role wins in an unusual way (neutrals and such)
#   <Section>.Help      One to three sentences per button. <Section> is the button's name key (order = HelpSections in the role class). Parts that aren't buttons can be sections too
#   <Section>.Short     One short line shown next to the button picture in Match Info. Tapping it opens <Section>.Help
#   <Role>.Tips         How to play it, or how it interacts with other roles (optional)
#   <Role>.Quote        A closing line shown last
# Setting values are listed under the description automatically, so don't repeat them in the text. Add-ons only need a short <Role>.Help.

# ── Demolisher ──
Demolisher.Name: Demolisher
Demolisher.Blurb: Smash walls to open new paths
Demolisher.Summary: A crewmate who can smash walls to open new paths through the ship.
Demolisher.Hammer.Help: Smash the wall in front of you. The wall crumbles on everyone's screen and becomes a path. Portals and drafting desks break after three hits too.
Demolisher.Hammer.Short: Smash the wall you face
Demolisher.Tips: Every new path is both an escape route and a shortcut, for impostors as well.
Demolisher.Quote: If there's a wall, break it.
Demolisher.SmashCooldown: Hammer Cooldown
Demolisher.SmashUses: Hammer Uses (0 = unlimited)
Demolisher.Hammer: Hammer

# ── Lighter ──
Lighter.Name: Lighter
Lighter.Blurb: See further than the rest
Lighter.Summary: A crewmate who sees farther than others.
Lighter.Tips: Keep watch from afar and report what you saw in meetings.
Lighter.Quote: Nothing hides in the dark from me.
Lighter.VisionMultiplier: Vision Multiplier
Lighter.VisionMultiplier.Detail: Multiplier applied to normal crewmate vision.

# ── Portal Maker (PortalMaker) ──
PortalMaker.Name: Portal Maker
PortalMaker.Blurb: Link two places with portals
PortalMaker.Summary: A crewmate who can link two distant places with portals.
PortalMaker.Portal.Help: Place a portal at your feet. If a vent, console, door, or ladder is too close, it goes to the nearest open spot. Once two are placed, any living player can stand on one and press Use to travel to the other. Press again after placing both to remove them and place again. The settings decide whether they can be removed.
PortalMaker.Portal.Short: Place at your feet. Two make a link
PortalMaker.NoRoom: No room to place a portal nearby
PortalMaker.Tips: Impostors can use the portals too. A portal breaks after three hits from the Demolisher's hammer.
PortalMaker.Quote: No more long way around.
PortalMaker.PlaceCooldown: Portal Cooldown
PortalMaker.CanRemove: Press Again to Remove Portals
PortalMaker.CanRemove.Detail: When OFF, pressing again after placing both portals does not remove them, so they cannot be placed again.
PortalMaker.Portal: Portal

# ── Rewinder ──
Rewinder.Name: Rewinder
Rewinder.Blurb: Turn back time and undo what happened
Rewinder.Summary: A crewmate who can turn the ship's time back a few seconds.
Rewinder.Rewind.Help: Hold the button to raise the seconds to turn back, one per second from 3; release it to use. Returns everyone's position, life or death, task progress, cooldowns and sabotages to how they were a few seconds ago. Anyone killed in that time comes back to life. You go back too; only this button's uses and cooldown stay as they are.
Rewinder.Rewind.Short: Hold, then release to turn time back
Rewinder.Tips: You cannot go back to before the last meeting. When time turns back, everyone's screen flashes for a moment, but no one can tell who did it.
Rewinder.Quote: That moment never happened.
Rewinder.Seconds: Max Seconds to Turn Back
Rewinder.Seconds.Detail: While you hold the button, the rewind grows from 3 seconds by 1 second at a time, up to this limit.
Rewinder.Cooldown: Rewind Cooldown
Rewinder.Uses: Rewind Uses (0 = unlimited)
Rewinder.Rewind: Rewind

# ── Architect ──
Architect.Name: Architect
Architect.Blurb: Reshape the ship from your blueprint
Architect.Summary: An impostor who can draw lines on a blueprint to raise walls in the ship.
Architect.Desk.Help: Place a drafting desk just behind your feet. If walls or consoles are in the way, it goes to the nearest open spot. Everyone can see the desks, and anyone can use them. A desk breaks after three hits from the Demolisher's hammer or when caught in an explosion, and a broken one cannot be placed again.
Architect.Desk.Short: Place a desk to open the blueprint
Architect.DeskNoRoom: No room to place a desk nearby
Architect.Plan.Help: Press it in front of a desk to open a top-down blueprint of where the ship can be walked. Other players appear as colorless shadows. Hold and drag to draw a line; release to raise walls from the floor along it. You can only draw inside the circle your desk reaches, and only as far as your gauge allows. The gauge refills over time. Anyone standing where a wall rises is pushed aside. Walls crumble after a while and can also be broken by hammers and explosions. While the blueprint is open you cannot move or kill.
Architect.Plan.Short: Draw a line to raise a wall
Architect.Pipe: Pipes
Architect.Pipe.Help: Tap near a wall of a water room (teal on the blueprint) to spend more gauge and burst the pipe inside the wall, spraying water. Water on the floor also shows on the blueprint.
Architect.Pipe.Short: Burst a pipe in a water-room wall
Architect.Drone: Drone
Architect.Drone.Help: While the blueprint is open, a drone flies out from the desk, picks up large rubble inside the circle and brings it back to refill the gauge. The drone also shows on the blueprint.
Architect.Drone.Short: Brings back rubble to refill the gauge
Architect.Tips: When someone else uses one of your desks, your blueprint closes and they can draw walls with your gauge.
Architect.Quote: I decide what shape this ship takes.
Architect.DeskCount: Desks
Architect.DeskCooldown: Desk Cooldown
Architect.GaugeLength: Wall Gauge (Length)
Architect.GaugeLength.Detail: Drawing a wall uses up gauge equal to the length drawn. This sets how much a full gauge holds.
Architect.GaugeRefill: Gauge Refill Time
Architect.WallLife: Wall Lifetime
Architect.WallLife.Detail: Walls you raise crumble after this long.
Architect.PipeCost: Pipe Burst Cost
Architect.PipeCost.Detail: Gauge used to burst a water pipe once. Same unit as wall length.
Architect.OwnRubble: Rubble From Own Walls
Architect.OwnRubble.Detail: When ON, the drone can also bring back rubble from your own walls that crumbled with time, refilling the gauge.
Architect.Desk: Desk
Architect.Plan: Blueprint
Architect.UseDesk: Use Desk

# ── Quickdraw ──
Quickdraw.Name: Quickdraw
Quickdraw.Blurb: Strike again before anyone else
Quickdraw.Summary: An impostor whose kill cooldown is shorter than the room setting.
Quickdraw.Tips: After a kill, go for the next one before anyone gets suspicious.
Quickdraw.Quote: Quickest on the draw, quickest to finish.
Quickdraw.KillCooldown: Kill Cooldown
Quickdraw.KillCooldownMode: Kill Cooldown Type
Quickdraw.KillCooldownMode.Detail: When based on the room value (the Kill Cooldown in game settings), the Quickdraw cooldown follows when the room value changes. The number in brackets is the result with the current room value.
Quickdraw.KillCooldownOffset: Seconds Added to Room Value
Quickdraw.KillCooldownRatio: Multiplier on Room Value
CooldownMode.Fixed: Fixed
CooldownMode.Offset: Room value ± sec
CooldownMode.Ratio: Room value ×

# ── Jester ──
Jester.Name: Jester
Jester.Blurb: Get yourself voted out
Jester.Summary: A neutral who wins by getting voted out in a meeting.
Jester.WinCond: Get voted out in a meeting to win alone
Jester.Tips: You cannot kill. Act suspicious and draw the votes.
Jester.Quote: A jester's finest hour is on the gallows.

# ── Outlaw ──
Outlaw.Name: Outlaw
Outlaw.Blurb: Be the last one standing
Outlaw.Summary: A neutral who can kill while looking like a crewmate.
Outlaw.WinCond: Win when no impostors are left and the remaining survivors are no more than the Outlaws
Outlaw.Kill: Kill
Outlaw.Kill.Help: You have the regular kill button. Kill cooldown, vision and kill distance are set under "Neutrals" in the Game Settings tab.
Outlaw.Kill.Short: You have the kill button
Outlaw.Tips: Impostors are your enemies too.
Outlaw.Quote: No law, no friends, no need.
