# ── Survivor ──
Survivor.Name: Survivor
Survivor.Blurb: Stay alive until the end
Survivor.Summary: A neutral who wins by staying alive until the end.
Survivor.WinCond: Win with whoever wins, as long as you are alive at the end of the game
Survivor.Tips: You cannot kill. Use your vest when in danger, and stay out of every team's way.
Survivor.Quote: Whoever wins, staying alive is my victory.
Survivor.Vest: Vest
Survivor.Vest.Help: Put on a vest for a set time to block kills. Blocking a kill restarts the attacker's kill cooldown. The vest comes off when a meeting starts. It does not stop abilities that kill without leaving a body (such as blasts).
Survivor.Vest.Short: Block kills for a while
Survivor.VestSaved: Your vest blocked a kill
Survivor.VestCooldown: Vest cooldown
Survivor.VestDuration: Vest duration
Survivor.MaxVests: Number of vests

# ── Samurai ──
Samurai.Name: Samurai
Samurai.Blurb: Draw your blade and cut down those who deserve it
Samurai.Epithet: Aurora Avenger
Epithet.Wayfinder: Wayfinder
Samurai.Summary: A neutral who cuts with a katana. Anyone who can fight back is drawn into a duel and worn down until they fall.
Samurai.WinCond: Path of the Guardian: cut down the set number of Impostors, then win with the Crewmates if you are alive when they win. Path of Carnage: win alone by cutting down enough players after falling, or when at most one other player is left alive (if that player is an Impostor, the fight goes on until one of you falls)
Samurai.Draw: Iaido and Sheathing
Samurai.Draw.Help: Your katana normally stays in its sheath, and you look like any other Crewmate. Hold the left mouse button on PC, or press and hold the right half of the screen on mobile, to charge an iaido strike, then swipe to draw and cut in one motion. Keyboard only: hold the Ability 1 key (Z by default) to charge, and release it to draw and cut toward the direction you are walking. The longer you charge, the harder it cuts. An iaido strike drawn with plenty of Spirit left leaves its cut behind as a rift in space. The view on the two sides of a rift slides in opposite directions along the line, and anyone standing across it looks split in two at the rift. Only the view changes; nobody actually moves. Rifts close at the same time cut doors return. A fully charged iaido strike landed outside a duel fells anyone in one cut, and fells anyone who cannot fight back in one cut even during a duel. Right-click or press the Ability 2 key (X by default) on PC, or tap the sheath button on mobile, to sheathe your katana. While drawn, everyone can see your katana. It is sheathed again after each meeting.
Samurai.Draw.Short: Charge and swipe to draw and cut at once
Samurai.Slash: Slash
Samurai.Slash.Help: While your katana is drawn, hold the left mouse button and move the mouse on PC, or drag on the right half of the screen on mobile, and the katana follows your motion. Faster swings cut harder. Push straight out from your body quickly to thrust instead: it reaches farther in a narrow line and carries you a short step forward. Push out while sheathed to thrust as you draw. Keyboard only: press the Ability 1 key (Z by default) to sweep across the direction you are walking, and keep pressing to alternate left and right. Press the Ability 3 key (C by default) to thrust toward the direction you are walking. Anyone you cut enters a duel with you, losing health with each cut and falling at zero. This includes those who cannot fight back. If the Impostor you are dueling kills you while you have more than half your health left, you lose 50 health instead of dying. While your katana is drawn, an Impostor cannot kill you in one blow; their kill starts a duel instead. It does not reach through walls. Press Shift on PC (the dash button on mobile) to dash toward the mouse (your walking direction on mobile, or after a keyboard cut). If there is ground you cannot walk to in that direction, such as the other end of a ladder or moving platform, or the top or bottom of a cliff, you leap there instead. You can leap even with your blade sheathed. You cannot walk with the mouse, so walk with the keys. Whoever you cut can leap back during the duel to avoid your strikes. They can store up to 2 leaps, and each used leap comes back after 3 seconds. When your blade keeps meeting another Samurai's, you lock blades: mash Left Click or Space on PC, or tap the screen on mobile, to push through. Cutting a door breaks it, and it cannot be closed (not even by door sabotage) until it comes back.
Samurai.Slash.Short: Swipe to swing and wear down health
Samurai.Ki: Spirit
Samurai.Ki.Help: Every swing and dash spends spirit, shown as the ring at your feet. Keep swinging without letting go and every swing after the first costs less. Spirit refills quickly while sheathed, slowly while you stand still with your katana drawn, and even more slowly while walking. Run out and your katana droops, leaving you unable to act for a moment. The back of the ring is notched with how many you have cut down.
Samurai.Ki.Short: Each swing spends spirit; run dry and you are open
Samurai.Paths: Guardian and Carnage
Samurai.Paths.Help: You start on the Path of the Guardian. Cutting down the set number of non-Impostors makes you fall to the Path of Carnage, and you can no longer win as a Guardian. Only you are told that you have fallen. Once you master the Guardian path or fall to Carnage, you can use your finishing move once per game. Keep holding after your draw is fully charged and your aura swells, turning gold on the Guardian path or crimson on the Path of Carnage. Draw then to cut down everyone around you at once.
Samurai.Paths.Short: Who you cut decides your path
Samurai.Tips: Drawing your katana reveals what you are. To the Crewmates, a Samurai who cuts down Impostors is a strong ally.
Samurai.Quote: Once drawn, the blade must cut.
Samurai.PathKills: Impostors to cut for the Guardian path
Samurai.FallKills: Non-Impostors cut before falling to Carnage
Samurai.CarnageShare: Cuts needed to win on Carnage (share of players alive when you fell)
Samurai.AnnounceSlot: Tell everyone a Wayfinder is in the match (without saying who)
Epithet.Announce: A {name} sails with this crew
Samurai.AnnounceFall: Tell everyone when the Samurai falls
Samurai.SlashRange: Slash Range
Samurai.CutRestore: Cut Doors and Rifts Return
Samurai.CutRestoreMeeting: At the next meeting
Samurai.CutRestoreSeconds: After a time
Samurai.CutRestoreNever: Never
Samurai.CutRestoreTime: Seconds Until Cut Doors and Rifts Return
Samurai.PathDesc: Path of the Guardian: Impostors cut {n}/{max}
Samurai.FallenDesc: Path of Carnage: cut down since falling {n}/{max}
Samurai.PathNotice: <color=#4A8CFF>You have mastered the Guardian path. Survive and win with the Crewmates</color>
Samurai.FellNotice: <color=#C0203A>You have fallen to Carnage. You can no longer win with anyone</color>
Samurai.FellAnnounce: <color=#C0203A>The Samurai has fallen to Carnage</color>

# ── Hawkeye ──
Hawkeye.Name: Hawkeye
Hawkeye.Blurb: See further than the rest
Hawkeye.Help: An add-on that widens your vision. The settings decide which teams can get it.
Hawkeye.VisionPercent: Vision
Hawkeye.VisionPercent.Detail: Vision of the holder, where normal vision is 100%.

# ── Quickhands ──
Quickhands.Name: Quickhands
Quickhands.Blurb: Strike again sooner
Quickhands.Help: An add-on that shortens your kill cooldown. Only players who can kill (impostors and roles with a kill button) can get it.
Quickhands.Reduction: Cooldown Reduction
Quickhands.Reduction.Detail: Shortens the kill cooldown by this much. 20% of 30 seconds gives 24 seconds.

# ── Sensitive ──
Sensitive.Name: Sensitive
Sensitive.Blurb: Sense it when someone falls
Sensitive.Help: When someone is killed, your screen alone flashes red for a moment. It does not tell you who or where.
Sensitive.Strength: Flash Strength
Sensitive.Strength.Detail: How strongly the screen flashes red when someone is killed.

# ── Autopsy ──
Autopsy.Name: Autopsy
Autopsy.Blurb: The dead tell tales
Autopsy.Help: An add-on that shows how each dead player died on their meeting nameplate: killed, ejected, or by their own hand.
Autopsy.ShowKillerRole: See the killer's role
Autopsy.ShowKillerRole.Detail: Adds the killer's role to the cause of death. The killer's name is not shown.
Autopsy.OnBodies: Show on bodies during the round
Autopsy.OnBodies.Detail: Shows the cause of death above nearby bodies before a meeting. Bodies behind walls do not show it.
Autopsy.Killed: Killed
Autopsy.KilledByRole: Killed by {role}
Autopsy.Suicide: Own hand
Autopsy.Exiled: Ejected
Autopsy.Spaced: Spaced
Autopsy.Left: Disconnected

# ── Baiting ──
Baiting.Name: Baiting
Baiting.Blurb: Who fell into the trap?
Baiting.Help: An add-on that makes your killer report your body shortly after the kill.
Baiting.ReportTime: Time until report
Baiting.ReportTime.Detail: Seconds after the kill until the killer reports the body.
Baiting.WarnKiller: Flash the killer's screen
Baiting.WarnKiller.Detail: Flashes the killer's screen cyan so they know they killed a Baiting player.
Baiting.RandomDelay: Randomize the report delay
Baiting.DelayVariation: Maximum extra delay
Baiting.DelayVariation.Detail: Adds a random 0 to this many seconds to the report delay.
Baiting.KnowSelf: Know you have Baiting
Baiting.KnowSelf.Detail: A ◎ appears next to your own name.
Baiting.EveryoneKnows: Everyone knows
Baiting.EveryoneKnows.Detail: A ◎ appears next to Baiting players' names on everyone's screen.

