# ════ SuperNewRoles から移した役職 ════
# ── メイヤー (Mayor) ──
Mayor.Name: Mayor
Mayor.Blurb: That power will save the village
Mayor.Summary: A crewmate who casts more votes than anyone else in meetings.
Mayor.Votes: Number of votes
# ── マッドメイト (Madmate) ──
Madmate.Name: Madmate
Madmate.Blurb: One who has strayed from the path
Madmate.Summary: A crewmate on the impostors' side.
Madmate.WinCond: Win when the impostors win, dead or alive
Madmate.KnowImpostors: Can know the impostors
Madmate.NeededTasks: Tasks needed to know them
Madmate.CanVent: Can use vents
Madmate.ImpostorVision: Has impostor vision
Madmate.MaddenRoles: Crew roles can be Madmates
Madmate.MaddenRoles.Detail: Some crew roles can be handed out as Madmates, keeping their abilities. Set the chance and count in each role's settings. These Madmates also follow the Madmate settings above (knowing the impostors, vents, vision).
Madmate.Prefix: Mad-
RoleState.Changed: Your role is now {role}
# ── シェリフ (Sheriff) ──
Sheriff.Name: Sheriff
Sheriff.Blurb: In the name of justice
Sheriff.Summary: A crewmate who can execute a nearby player. If the target isn't on a team you may kill, you die instead.
Sheriff.Execute: Execute
Sheriff.Execute.Help: Kills a nearby player. If they aren't on a team you're allowed to kill, you die instead (depends on the suicide setting).
Sheriff.Execute.Short: Execute a nearby player
Sheriff.KillCooldown: Execute cooldown
Sheriff.MaxKills: Executions
Sheriff.SuicideMode: Suicide mode
Sheriff.SuicideMode.Default: Only on a wrong target
Sheriff.SuicideMode.AlwaysSuicide: Always die with the target
Sheriff.SuicideMode.AlwaysKill: Never die
Sheriff.KillImpostor: Can kill impostors
Sheriff.KillMad: Can kill madmates
Sheriff.KillNeutral: Can kill neutrals
Sheriff.KillFriends: Can kill friends
Sheriff.KillLovers: Can kill lovers
# ── 霊媒師 (Seer) ──
Seer.Name: Seer
Seer.Blurb: Hear the voices of souls
Seer.Summary: A crewmate whose screen flashes when someone dies and who sees souls where people died.
Seer.Mode: Mode
Seer.Mode.Both: Flash and souls
Seer.Mode.Flash: Flash only
Seer.Mode.Soul: Souls only
Seer.LimitSoul: Souls fade over time
Seer.SoulDuration: Soul duration
# ── ジャッカル (Jackal) ──
Jackal.Name: Jackal
Jackal.Blurb: Hunt everything with your pack
Jackal.Summary: A neutral killer who can recruit a partner once.
Jackal.WinCond: Win when only the Jackal's pack is left alive
Jackal.Kill: Kill
Jackal.Kill.Help: Has the vanilla kill button. Vision and kill distance follow the Neutral settings in the Game Settings tab. Cannot kill your pack.
Jackal.Kill.Short: Has the kill button
Jackal.Sidekick: Sidekick
Jackal.Sidekick.Help: Turns a nearby player into your partner (Sidekick or Jackal Friends), once.
Jackal.Sidekick.Short: Recruit a nearby player
Jackal.KillCooldown: Kill cooldown
Jackal.CanVent: Can use vents
Jackal.CanSidekick: Can recruit
Jackal.SidekickCooldown: Recruit cooldown
Jackal.Infinite: Promoted Jackals can recruit too
# ── サイドキック (Sidekick) ──
Sidekick.Name: Sidekick
Sidekick.Blurb: The Jackal's right hand
Sidekick.Summary: A neutral recruited by the Jackal. Cannot kill, and becomes a Jackal when all Jackals are dead.
Sidekick.WinCond: Win when the Jackal wins
Sidekick.CanVent: Can use vents
# ── ラバーズ (Lovers) ──
Lovers.Name: Lovers
Lovers.Blurb: Our love is forever
Lovers.Summary: An add-on given to a pair. You know your partner (♥ by their name), and you die when they die.
Lovers.WinCond: If both are alive at the end, you steal the win together
Lovers.FollowDeath: Die when your partner dies
Lovers.SoloWin: Steal the win if both are alive
# ── ヴァルチャー (Vulture) ──
Vulture.Name: Vulture
Vulture.Blurb: Feast on the dead
Vulture.Summary: A neutral who eats bodies to erase them. Eat enough to win alone.
Vulture.WinCond: Win alone the moment you've eaten enough bodies
Vulture.Eat: Eat
Vulture.Eat.Help: Eats and removes a body within report range. You see arrows to bodies (option).
Vulture.Eat.Short: Eat a nearby body
Vulture.Cooldown: Eat cooldown
Vulture.RequiredBodies: Bodies needed to win
Vulture.CanVent: Can use vents
Vulture.Count: Bodies eaten {n}/{max}
# ── アーソニスト (Arsonist) ──
Arsonist.Name: Arsonist
Arsonist.Blurb: Burn it all to ashes
Arsonist.Summary: A neutral who wins by dousing everyone in oil and setting it alight.
Arsonist.WinCond: Win alone by dousing every living player and igniting
Arsonist.Douse: Douse
Arsonist.Douse.Help: Stay next to a nearby person for a moment to douse them. Moving away or a different nearest person cancels it. Doused people are marked §.
Arsonist.Douse.Short: Douse a nearby player
Arsonist.Ignite: Ignite
Arsonist.Ignite.Help: If every other living player is doused, ignite to win alone.
Arsonist.Ignite.Short: Ignite to win once all are doused
Arsonist.Cooldown: Douse cooldown
Arsonist.CanVent: Can use vents
Arsonist.ImpostorVision: Has impostor vision
# ── カモフラージャー (Camouflager) ──
Camouflager.Name: Camouflager
Camouflager.Blurb: Who is who?
Camouflager.Summary: An impostor who can make everyone look like them for a while.
Camouflager.Camo: Camouflage
Camouflager.Camo.Help: For a set time, every living player looks like you.
Camouflager.Camo.Short: Make everyone look alike
Camouflager.Cooldown: Camouflage cooldown
Camouflager.Duration: Camouflage duration
# ── トリガーハッピー (TriggerHappy) ──
TriggerHappy.Name: Trigger Happy
TriggerHappy.Blurb: Shoot, shoot, and keep shooting
TriggerHappy.Summary: An impostor who sprays a machine gun for a while and kills anyone hit by enough bullets.
TriggerHappy.Spray: Spray
TriggerHappy.Spray.Help: Hold a machine gun for a while. On PC, hold the right mouse button to raise it, and hold the left mouse button to fire toward the mouse. Keyboard only: press the spray key to raise it, and keep holding it to fire in the direction you are walking. On mobile, touch the right half of the screen to bring up a stick, and it fires in that direction only while you tilt the stick. Anyone hit enough times dies. Bullets ricochet off walls (the number of bounces can be set), and keeping fire on one spot chips the wall until it breaks open.
TriggerHappy.Spray.Short: Spray the machine gun
TriggerHappy.Cooldown: Spray cooldown
TriggerHappy.Range: Bullet range
# ── ミラージュ (Mirage) ──
RolePicker.Crew: Crew
RolePicker.Impostor: Impostor
RolePicker.Neutral: Neutral
RolePicker.Close: Close
RolePicker.SearchHint: Search roles
RolePicker.NoMatch: No matching roles
RolePicker.Pick: Pick a role
RolePicker.Confirm: Press {role} again to shoot
GuessKit.Hit: {name} was shot
GuessKit.Missed: {name} guessed wrong and was shot
# ── ナイスゲッサー (NiceGuesser) ──
NiceGuesser.Name: Nice Guesser
NiceGuesser.Blurb: I see what you really are
NiceGuesser.Summary: A crewmate who can shoot by guessing roles in meetings. A wrong guess kills them.
NiceGuesser.Shoot: Shoot
NiceGuesser.Shoot.Help: In a meeting, pick a player and guess their role. If right, they die; if wrong, you die.
NiceGuesser.Shoot.Short: Guess a role and shoot
NiceGuesser.Shots: Total shots
NiceGuesser.PerMeeting: Shots per meeting
# ── イビルゲッサー (EvilGuesser) ──
EvilGuesser.Name: Evil Guesser
EvilGuesser.Blurb: The meeting is my hunting ground
EvilGuesser.Summary: An impostor who can shoot by guessing roles in meetings. A wrong guess kills them.
EvilGuesser.Shoot: Shoot
EvilGuesser.Shoot.Help: In a meeting, pick a player and guess their role. If right, they die; if wrong, you die.
EvilGuesser.Shoot.Short: Guess a role and shoot
EvilGuesser.Shots: Total shots
EvilGuesser.PerMeeting: Shots per meeting
# ── ホスフォラス (Phosphorus) ──
Phosphorus.Name: Phosphorus
Phosphorus.Blurb: A lantern against the dark
Phosphorus.Summary: A crewmate who places lanterns and lights them up.
Phosphorus.Put: Place
Phosphorus.Put.Help: Places a lantern where you stand. Everyone can see it from the next round. If an explosion or a blow knocks it over, it breaks and spills oil, which catches fire if the lantern was lit.
Phosphorus.Put.Short: Place a lantern
Phosphorus.Light: Light
Phosphorus.Light.Help: Lights your lanterns for a while, brightening their surroundings (press again to turn off). Walls block the light, but it leaks through holes in them. A lantern goes out under water and lights up by itself near fire.
Phosphorus.Light.Short: Light the lanterns
Phosphorus.Cooldown: Place cooldown
Phosphorus.Limit: Lantern limit
Phosphorus.LightCooldown: Light cooldown
Phosphorus.Duration: Light duration
Phosphorus.Range: Light range
# ── マッシュルーマー (Mushroomer) ──
Mushroomer.Name: Mushroomer
Mushroomer.Blurb: Smother them in spores
Mushroomer.Summary: An impostor who plants mushrooms and makes every mushroom on the ship burst with spores. Works on any map.
Mushroomer.Plant: Plant
Mushroomer.Plant.Help: Plants a mushroom at your feet. It becomes active after the next meeting (impostors see it faintly).
Mushroomer.Plant.Short: Plant a mushroom
Mushroomer.Explode: Burst
Mushroomer.Explode.Help: Usable once all your mushrooms are planted and active. Every active mushroom on the ship bursts with spores at once.
Mushroomer.Explode.Short: Burst all mushrooms
Mushroomer.HasGasMask: Has a gas mask
Mushroomer.PlantCooldown: Plant cooldown
Mushroomer.PlantCount: Mushrooms to plant
Mushroomer.ExplodeCooldown: Burst cooldown
Mushroomer.ExplodeCount: Burst uses
Mushroomer.ExplodeRange: Spore range
Mushroomer.ExplodeDuration: Spore duration
Mushroomer.ActiveUsedMushroom: Planted mushrooms visible only to you
# ── リモコン (RemoteController) ──
RemoteController.Name: Remote Controller
RemoteController.Blurb: You move as I please
RemoteController.Summary: An impostor who controls a crewmate's movement and makes them kill.
RemoteController.Mark: Mark
RemoteController.Mark.Help: Picks a nearby crewmate to control.
RemoteController.Mark.Short: Pick who to control
RemoteController.Operate: Operate
RemoteController.Operate.Help: For a while (or without limit), you move the marked person. Neither of you can move on your own meanwhile. Press again to stop.
RemoteController.Operate.Short: Move the marked person
RemoteController.Kill: Remote Kill
RemoteController.Kill.Help: While operating: the person you control kills someone near them. Ends the operation.
RemoteController.Kill.Short: Make your puppet kill
RemoteController.MarkCooldown: Mark cooldown
RemoteController.OperationInfinite: Unlimited operation
RemoteController.OperationDuration: Operation duration
RemoteController.Controlled: Remote-controlled
RemoteController.ControlledUntil: you can't move on your own
# ── ロケットランチャー (RocketLauncher) ──
RocketLauncher.Name: Rocket Launcher
RocketLauncher.Blurb: Human rocket, launch!
RocketLauncher.Summary: An impostor who grabs a crewmate and launches them to explode on impact.
RocketLauncher.Load: Load
RocketLauncher.Load.Help: Grabs a nearby crewmate. They cannot move and are carried with you.
RocketLauncher.Load.Short: Grab a crewmate
RocketLauncher.Shot: Launch
RocketLauncher.Shot.Help: Launches the grabbed person where you aim: left-click on PC, or this button on mobile. On hitting a wall (or a person, by setting) they explode, killing those nearby. If a meeting starts, the held or flying person dies (a Samurai is just let go). A Samurai can break out of the cannon by swinging the sword a few times, and the blast does not kill them in one hit: they are knocked back and start a duel with you.
RocketLauncher.Shot.Short: Launch the grabbed person
RocketLauncher.Cooldown: Load cooldown
RocketLauncher.CollideWithPlayers: Explodes on hitting people
RocketLauncher.KillImpostors: Explosion kills impostors
RocketLauncher.ExplosionRange: Kill radius
RocketLauncher.LaunchSpeed: Launch speed
RocketLauncher.WallBlastSize: Wall blast size
RocketLauncher.WallBlastPower: Wall blast power
RocketLauncher.LimitLoadedTime: Limit holding time
RocketLauncher.LoadedTimeLimit: Holding time
RocketLauncher.CanUseNormalKill: Can kill normally
# ── 突き落と師 (Pusher) ──
Pusher.Name: Pusher
Pusher.Blurb: Watch your step
Pusher.Summary: An impostor who pushes people standing at the ship's edges or atop ladders (Skeld, Polus, Airship, Fungle).
Pusher.Push: Push
Pusher.Push.Help: Pushes a crewmate standing at a ship edge (fixed spots). They fall and leave no body. Pushing someone atop a ladder leaves their body at the bottom.
Pusher.Push.Short: Push someone off an edge
Pusher.Cooldown: Push cooldown
# ── ユビキタス (Ubiquitous) ──
Ubiquitous.Name: Ubiquitous
Ubiquitous.Blurb: Drones are everywhere
Ubiquitous.Summary: A crewmate who flies a drone to watch and open doors.
Ubiquitous.Call: Call / Return
Ubiquitous.Call.Help: Spawns a drone at your feet. Press again to remove it. When a meeting starts, a flying drone stops where it is and stays for the set number of meetings. People near your stopped drones show on the map.
Ubiquitous.Call.Short: Call a drone
Ubiquitous.Operate: Operate
Ubiquitous.Operate.Help: Pilot the drone. You cannot move while doing so; the camera follows the drone and you can see around it.
Ubiquitous.Operate.Short: Fly the drone
Ubiquitous.DoorHack: Hack Doors
Ubiquitous.DoorHack.Help: While piloting, opens closed doors near the drone.
Ubiquitous.DoorHack.Short: Open nearby doors
Ubiquitous.CallCooldown: Call cooldown
Ubiquitous.OperateCooldown: Operate cooldown
Ubiquitous.LimitOperate: Limit operating time
Ubiquitous.OperateTime: Operating time
Ubiquitous.StayTurns: Meetings a drone stays
Ubiquitous.FlyingSpeed: Drone speed
Ubiquitous.DoorHackCooldown: Door hack cooldown
Ubiquitous.DoorHackScope: Door hack range
Ubiquitous.VisibilityRange: Drone vision range
Ubiquitous.MapShowColor: Show colors on the map
Ubiquitous.ShowFlying: Show flying drones to everyone
# ── 作り直し: シーア / イビルシーア / ヴァルチャー / アーソニスト / マトリョーシカ / 魔術師 ──
EvilSeer.LightColor: a light color
EvilSeer.DarkColor: a dark color
EvilSeer.FlashColorText: Someone of {color} died
Vulture.ShowArrows: Show arrows to bodies
Arsonist.Duration: Douse time
# ── 作り直し: ジャンボ ──
TriggerHappy.Unlimited: Unlimited uses
TriggerHappy.UseLimit: Uses
TriggerHappy.SyncKillCooldown: Sync spray and kill cooldowns
TriggerHappy.Duration: Spray duration
TriggerHappy.RequiredHits: Hits needed to kill
TriggerHappy.BulletSize: Bullet size
TriggerHappy.PierceWalls: Bullets pierce walls
TriggerHappy.Ricochets: Ricochets off walls
TriggerHappy.SpreadAngle: Bullet spread
TriggerHappy.FriendlyFire: Friendly fire
TriggerHappy.KillSound: Play kill sound
Null.Name: Null
Null.Blurb: Be no one, become someone
Null.Summary: A neutral who wins by surviving after spending time with others, then time alone.
Null.WinCond: Finish both phases and be alive at the end (steal the win or join the winners, by setting)
Null.Phase1: Together
Null.Phase1.Help: Time builds up while someone is within range. When it reaches the set time, phase 2 begins.
Null.Phase1.Short: Stay near someone to build time
Null.Phase2: Alone
Null.Phase2.Help: Time builds up while no one is within range. When it reaches the set time, the condition is met.
Null.Phase2.Short: Stay alone to build time
Null.Achieved: Null condition met. Survive to win
Null.Achieved.Label: Done
Null.Phase2Started: Phase 2: now stay alone
Null.Status1: Time together {n}/{max} s
Null.Status2: Time alone {n}/{max} s
Null.Tips: The button fill and the task list show your progress. Built-up time never goes down.
Null.SoloWin: Steal the win alone
Null.TogetherRange: Range counted as together
Null.AloneRange: Range counted as alone
Null.TogetherTime: Time needed together
Null.AloneTime: Time needed alone
FakeJester.Name: Fake Jester
FakeJester.Blurb: A fake who played the fool
FakeJester.Summary: A neutral who believes they are the Jester. After a set number of meetings, they realize their true role.
FakeJester.WinCond: After realizing, win by being alive at the end (being voted out is not a win)
FakeJester.Tips: Until you realize, you will act like a Jester. After that, aim to survive.
FakeJester.Awaken: You were never the Jester... you are the Fake Jester! Survive to win
FakeJester.AwakenedLabel: Jester/Fake Jester
FakeJester.AwakenMeetings: Meetings until realizing
FakeJester.AdditionalWin: Join the winners
Guardian.Name: Guardian
Guardian.Blurb: My body as your shield
Guardian.Summary: A crewmate who protects a chosen player in meetings and dies in their place when they are attacked.
Guardian.Guard: Guard
Guardian.Guard.Help: In a meeting, pick a player with the button on their nameplate (after finishing the set number of tasks). If they are about to be killed, they survive and the Guardian dies instead. If a guesser shoots them, the shooter dies. Against an Alchemist's alchemy bullet, the Guardian dies in their place as with other kills. The guard ends after the set number of meetings.
Guardian.Guard.Short: Die in place of the player you chose
Guardian.Tips: Guard players who seem likely to be targeted. Your sacrifice is announced at the next meeting.
Guardian.StartGuarding: Started guarding {name}
Guardian.YouAreGuarded: You are being guarded by a Guardian
Guardian.GuardExpired: Your Guardian's protection has ended
Guardian.GuardExpiredSelf: Your guard on {name} has ended
Guardian.SacrificeAnnounce: A Guardian died in place of {name}
Guardian.Duration: Meetings a guard lasts
Guardian.Simultaneous: Players guarded at once
Guardian.Lifetime: Players guarded per match
Guardian.RequiredTasks: Tasks needed to guard
Comet.Name: Comet
Comet.Blurb: Blaze through
Comet.Summary: A crewmate who can turn invisible and run fast.
Comet.Blaze: Blaze
Comet.Blaze.Help: Become invisible and faster for a set time (your vision widens and the screen zooms out a little). While invisible you cannot be seen or killed.
Comet.Blaze.Short: Turn invisible and run fast
Comet.Tips: Not affected by lights sabotage.
Comet.Cooldown: Boost cooldown
Comet.Duration: Boost duration
Comet.Speed: Boost speed
Comet.Vision: Vision during boost
Comet.Screen: Screen zoom during boost
Alchemist.Name: Alchemist
Alchemist.Blurb: Harmony toward death
Alchemist.Summary: A crewmate who turns bodies into alchemy bullets and shoots players in meetings.
Alchemist.Alchemy: Alchemy
Alchemist.Alchemy.Help: Remove a nearby body and turn it into the set number of alchemy bullets.
Alchemist.Alchemy.Short: Turn a body into bullets
Alchemist.Shoot: Shoot
Alchemist.Shoot.Help: In a meeting, shoot the player chosen with the button on their nameplate (up to the per-meeting limit). Players a guesser cannot shoot cannot be shot. If the target is guarded by a Guardian, the Guardian dies in their place (unlike a guesser, you do not die).
Alchemist.Shoot.Short: Shoot with alchemy bullets in meetings
Alchemist.Tips: Removed bodies can no longer be reported. Choose your targets carefully.
Alchemist.Bullets: Alchemy bullets: {n}
Alchemist.Hit: {name} was shot by an alchemy bullet
Alchemist.AlchemyCooldown: Alchemy cooldown
Alchemist.PerAlchemy: Bullets per alchemy
Alchemist.PerMeeting: Shots per meeting
Eclipse.Name: Eclipse
Eclipse.Blurb: Disaster rains down
Eclipse.Summary: An impostor who drops a meteor on a marked spot to kill everyone around it.
Eclipse.Mark: Mark
Eclipse.Mark.Help: Place a meteor mark at your feet (only you can see it). You stop briefly and a sound plays.
Eclipse.Mark.Short: Mark where the meteor falls
Eclipse.Blast: Meteor
Eclipse.Blast.Help: Drop a meteor on the mark. A red warning circle appears for everyone, then it falls and kills everyone inside, allies and yourself included.
Eclipse.Blast.Short: Drop a meteor on the mark
Eclipse.Tips: The meteor hits allies and you too. The warning circle lets people escape, so do not wait too long.
Eclipse.Uses: Meteor uses
Eclipse.MarkCooldown: Mark cooldown
Eclipse.BlastCooldown: Meteor cooldown
Eclipse.WarningTime: Warning time before impact
Eclipse.MarkStop: Stop time when marking
Eclipse.Size: Meteor size
Eclipse.ResetBlastCool: Marking resets meteor cooldown
Eclipse.MeetingReset: Meetings clear the mark
Eclipse.MarkSound: Mark sound heard by others
Eclipse.SoundRange: Mark sound range
Nova.Name: Nova
Nova.Blurb: The first cry of a star
Nova.Summary: An impostor who charges up and fires a straight beam that kills.
Nova.Fire: Fire
Nova.Fire.Help: Hold to charge in place, then release to fire a beam. The longer you charge, the wider the beam and the more people it can pierce. A quick tap stops at the first person hit; a full charge kills everyone in the beam. Walls stop the beam. You cannot move while charging, and your aim turns only slowly. Your charge shows in a tank beside you that others can see too. On PC, right-click to raise the cannon, hold left-click to charge, and release to fire toward the mouse. Right-click again while aiming to lower the cannon. On mobile, hold the button to charge and release to fire the way you last walked. The allowed directions depend on the setting.
Nova.Fire.Short: Charge and fire a beam
Nova.Tips: You cannot move while charging, and others can see how charged you are. A fully charged beam is especially strong in long corridors.
Nova.Mode: Fire mode
Nova.Mode.Free: Free (mouse direction)
Nova.Mode.LeftRight: Left/right (facing)
Nova.Mode.FourWay: Four directions
Nova.Mode.EightWay: Eight directions
Nova.Cooldown: Fire cooldown
Nova.Size: Beam width
Nova.Charge: Time to full charge
Nova.BeamColor: Beam Color
Nova.BeamColor.Mono: Black & White
Nova.BeamColor.Violet: Black & Violet
Scarlet.Name: Scarlet
Scarlet.Blurb: Still, I love you
Scarlet.Summary: A neutral who aims to win together with their favorite. Use your kept lovers well.
Scarlet.WinCond: When your favorite wins and both of you are alive (and the gauge is full), steal the win for the two of you
Scarlet.Keep: Keep
Scarlet.Keep.Help: Seduce a nearby player as a kept lover. You can see their role. Kept lovers do not die with you.
Scarlet.Keep.Short: Make a nearby player a kept lover
Scarlet.Favorite: Favorite
Scarlet.Favorite.Help: Make a nearby player your favorite (only one). If either of you dies, the other dies too.
Scarlet.Favorite.Short: Make a nearby player your favorite
Scarlet.Hourglass: Time left
Scarlet.Hourglass.Help: If you do not choose a favorite in time, you die of loneliness. The timer stops during meetings and shortly after. Once chosen, it becomes the favorite gauge.
Scarlet.Hourglass.Short: Time left to choose a favorite
Scarlet.Command: Command
Scarlet.Command.Help: In a meeting, issue the crimson command with the button on your own nameplate. Your favorite and kept lovers' votes go to your vote.
Scarlet.Command.Short: Make your lovers vote with you
Scarlet.Tips: The favorite gauge fills near your favorite and drains away from them. Your lovers cannot guess you.
Scarlet.Commanded: Crimson command issued. Your lovers' votes will follow yours
Scarlet.FavoriteChosen: {name} is now your favorite
Scarlet.KeptChosen: {name} is now kept
Scarlet.YouWereChosen: You were chosen as the Scarlet's lover
Scarlet.Gauge: Favorite gauge
Scarlet.GraceStatus: {n} s left to choose a favorite
Scarlet.FavoriteStatus: Favorite: {name}
Scarlet.GaugeStatus: Favorite: {name}  Gauge {n}%
Scarlet.Grace: Grace before choosing a favorite
Scarlet.NumOfKept: Max kept lovers
Scarlet.NumOfCommand: Max commands
Scarlet.CanOverrideTaskWin: Can steal task wins
Scarlet.WithGauge: Favorite gauge
Scarlet.RequiredGauge: Gauge needed to win
Scarlet.SurplusGauge: Surplus gauge
Scarlet.GaugeReduction: Gauge drain speed
Scarlet.CanLocateLovers: Show lovers' location
Scarlet.PreAssignedLovers: Pre-assigned lovers
Scarlet.Vent: Can use vents
Spectre.Name: Spectre
Spectre.Blurb: Grudge made flesh
Spectre.Summary: A neutral who steals the win by surviving to the end. But they starve without eating fried tofu for a while.
Spectre.WinCond: Alive at the end with more satiety than the set value: steal the win (not against sabotage wins)
Spectre.Vanish: Vanish
Spectre.Vanish.Help: Spend satiety to become invisible for a while. Usable only when at least one tofu's worth of satiety remains afterward.
Spectre.Vanish.Short: Spend satiety to turn invisible
Spectre.Eat: Fried tofu
Spectre.Eat.Help: Dishes on the map get fried tofu. Press near a dish with tofu to open the eating screen (click to bite). You starve when satiety runs out.
Spectre.Eat.Short: Eat the tofu on a dish
Spectre.Tips: Arrows show where killers are. You have impostor vision, ignore lights sabotage and can see through walls (by setting).
Spectre.Vent: Can use vents
Spectre.ShowKillers: Show killers' location
Spectre.Clairvoyance: Clairvoyance
Spectre.Immoralist: Follower assignment
Spectre.Immoralist.None: None
Spectre.Immoralist.Follower: Little Fox
Spectre.Immoralist.Immoralist: Immoralist
Spectre.Immoralist.Random: Random
Spectre.Immoralist.Alternate: Alternate
Spectre.FollowerChance: Little Fox chance (%)
Spectre.NumOfDishes: Max dishes
Spectre.SatietyRate: Satiety per tofu
Spectre.MaxSatiety: Max satiety
Spectre.InitialSatiety: Starting satiety
Spectre.RequiredSatiety: Satiety needed to win
Spectre.ShowDishesOnMap: Show tofu on the map
Spectre.Replenish: Tofu refill cooldown
Spectre.VanishCost: Vanish tofu cost
Spectre.VanishCooldown: Vanish cooldown
Spectre.VanishDuration: Vanish duration
Spectre.Adrenaline: Adrenaline mode
Spectre.AdrenalineRate: Satiety drain near killers
SpectreFollower.Name: Little Fox
SpectreFollower.Blurb: Dreaming of the great spirit
SpectreFollower.Summary: The Spectre's companion. Eats fried tofu to keep the Spectre's satiety up.
SpectreFollower.WinCond: Wins with the Spectre (dies when the Spectre dies)
SpectreFollower.Tips: The gauge at the bottom left shows the Spectre's satiety.
SpectreFollower.Vent: Can use vents
SpectreFollower.SatietyRate: Satiety per tofu
SpectreFollower.ShowDishesOnMap: Show tofu on the map
SpectreImmoralist.Name: Immoralist
SpectreImmoralist.Blurb: Walking the forbidden path
SpectreImmoralist.Summary: The Spectre's companion. While alive they offer fried tofu; after death they can remove it.
SpectreImmoralist.WinCond: Wins with the Spectre (dies when the Spectre dies)
SpectreImmoralist.Place: Offer
SpectreImmoralist.Place.Help: Press near an empty dish and wait there briefly to put tofu on it.
SpectreImmoralist.Place.Short: Offer tofu on an empty dish
SpectreImmoralist.Remove: Remove
SpectreImmoralist.Remove.Help: After death, remove tofu from dishes (while the Spectre is alive). Removing too much makes the Spectre starve.
SpectreImmoralist.Remove.Short: As a ghost, remove tofu
SpectreImmoralist.Suicide: Suicide
SpectreImmoralist.Suicide.Help: Kill yourself whenever you like.
SpectreImmoralist.Suicide.Short: Kill yourself
SpectreImmoralist.Vent: Can use vents
SpectreImmoralist.RespawnCooldown: Offer cooldown
SpectreImmoralist.RespawnDuration: Offer time
SpectreImmoralist.ShowDishesOnMap: Show tofu on the map
SpectreImmoralist.CanSuicide: Can kill self
SpectreImmoralist.ShowKillFlash: Show kill flash
Doppelganger.Name: Doppelganger
Doppelganger.Blurb: Me and my friend
Doppelganger.Summary: A crewmate who creates a phantom of themselves that can walk around and swap places with them.
Doppelganger.Command: Place
Doppelganger.Command.Help: Opens the map. The phantom walks where you click (it appears at your feet if there is none). The normal map works too. Players near the phantom show on the map.
Doppelganger.Command.Short: Walk the phantom from the map
Doppelganger.Swap: Swap
Doppelganger.Swap.Help: Stop in place for a moment, then swap places with the phantom.
Doppelganger.Swap.Short: Swap places with the phantom
Doppelganger.Despawn: Despawn
Doppelganger.Despawn.Help: Remove the phantom.
Doppelganger.Despawn.Short: Remove the phantom
Doppelganger.Tips: The phantom looks real to everyone. If it is killed, you die where the phantom was. It vanishes at meetings and when you die.
Doppelganger.NoPath: No path for the phantom to get there
Doppelganger.SwapBlocked: The phantom is inside an object, so you can't swap
Doppelganger.SwapCooldown: Swap cooldown
Doppelganger.SwapDuration: Swap time
Doppelganger.DetectionRadius: Phantom detection radius
IntroTeam.Neutral: Neutral
IntroTeam.NeutralSub: Neither Crewmate nor Impostor. Win your own way
IntroTeam.Madmate: Madmate
IntroTeam.MadmateSub: Blend in with the crew and help the Impostors win
