Ranked.PastimeShield: Shield!
Ranked.LeaveTitle: Leave the game?
Ranked.LeavePlaying: This ranked match is still going. Leaving now counts worse than a loss: your rank drops by {n}.
Ranked.LeaveLobby: You'll leave the ranked room (it's the lobby, so your rank won't drop).
Ranked.LeaveStay: Stay
Ranked.LeaveGo: Leave
Rank.Next: {n} more to {tier}
Rank.Top: Top rank
Ranked.SearchHint: While searching you cannot create or join other rooms
Ranked.Cancel: Cancel

# ---- Roles ported from Uchu and others (crew) ----
EmergencyLock.Locked: The emergency button is locked
Admiral.Name: Admiral
Admiral.Blurb: Take a roll call and find everyone
Admiral.Summary: A crewmate who can take a "Roll Call" during meetings. Living players answer by clicking where they are on the map, and when you close the call, pins in their colors appear on your map.
Admiral.Call: Roll Call
Admiral.Call.Help: Use it from your own plate during a meeting. Everyone's screen flashes and other living players get an "Answer" button (once per meeting).
Admiral.Call.Short: Ask everyone where they are
Admiral.Close: Close
Admiral.Close.Help: Closes the roll call. Each answer appears on the map as a pin in that player's color.
Admiral.Close.Short: Close the roll call
Admiral.NumOfCall: Number of roll calls
Admiral.VoteWatching: See votes even when voting is anonymous
Admiral.Answer: Roll call! Click where you are on the map to answer
Admiral.Answered: You answered the roll call
Admiral.Result: Roll call result: {n} answered (check the map)
Bakery.Name: Bakery
Bakery.Blurb: Hand out fresh bread
Bakery.Summary: A crewmate who can give bread to nearby players. Players holding bread get a bread mark on their meeting plate. While alive, you add a line to the exile screen.
Bakery.Give: Give
Bakery.Give.Help: Gives bread to a nearby player. You can give a set number per meeting; after the meeting the bread disappears and your count resets.
Bakery.Give.Short: Give bread to someone nearby
Bakery.GiveCooldown: Give cooldown
Bakery.BreadPerMeeting: Bread per meeting
Bakery.Got: You got some bread!
Bakery.Exile.Smell: There's a smell of baked dough...
Bakery.Exile.Burnt: The bread got burnt...
Bakery.Exile.Festival: It's a bread festival!
DJ.Name: DJ
DJ.Blurb: Turn the ship into a dance floor
DJ.Summary: A crewmate whose "Scratch" makes everyone in range (including you) flash in random colors.
DJ.Scratch: Scratch
DJ.Scratch.Help: Plays a scratch sound for everyone in range and flashes their screens in random colors several times. You briefly see the range circle.
DJ.Scratch.Short: Flash everyone nearby
DJ.ScratchCooldown: Scratch cooldown
DJ.Range: Range
DJ.NumOfFlash: Number of flashes
NiceDecorator.Name: Nice Decorator
NiceDecorator.Blurb: Decorate people and change their roles
NiceDecorator.Summary: A crewmate whose "Decorate" changes a nearby player's role. True crewmates get a random crew role and impostors a random impostor role (avoiding the one you gave last time). Neutrals and madmates are unaffected, but a use is spent.
NiceDecorator.Cooldown: Decorate cooldown
NiceDecorator.Uses: Decorate uses
EvilDecorator.Name: Evil Decorator
EvilDecorator.Blurb: Decorate people and change their roles
EvilDecorator.Summary: An impostor whose "Decorate" changes a nearby player's role. True crewmates get a random crew role and impostors a random impostor role (avoiding the one you gave last time). Neutrals and madmates are unaffected, but a use is spent.
EvilDecorator.Cooldown: Decorate cooldown
EvilDecorator.Uses: Decorate uses
Polaris.Name: Polaris
Polaris.Blurb: The North Star sees everything
Polaris.Summary: A crewmate with a kill that works on anyone, and a "Vision" that reads a dead player's role from their body.
Polaris.Kill: Kill
Polaris.Kill.Help: Kills a nearby player. You never die from a misfire.
Polaris.Kill.Short: Kill someone nearby
Polaris.KillCooldown: Kill cooldown
Polaris.KillUses: Kill uses
Polaris.CanKillHidden: Can also kill hidden players
Polaris.SealUntilReport: Seal the kill until a body is reported
Polaris.Vision: Vision
Polaris.Vision.Help: Gazes at a nearby body for a moment (you can't move). Afterwards, the next meeting shows you that player's name and role.
Polaris.Vision.Short: Read a body's role
Polaris.VisionCooldown: Vision cooldown
Polaris.VisionUses: Vision uses
Polaris.VisionDuration: Vision duration
Polaris.RewindTask: Vision undoes some of your tasks
Polaris.MediumRewindTask: Tasks undone
Polaris.Seen: You saw a vision. You'll learn more at the next meeting
Polaris.Result: Vision: {name} was {role}
Sonar.Name: Sonar
Sonar.Blurb: Report kills with trap antennas
Sonar.Summary: A crewmate who places antennas only they can see. When a kill happens right next to one, everyone gets an arrow and the antenna breaks.
Sonar.Place: Place
Sonar.Place.Help: Places an antenna at your feet. When a kill happens within its range outside a meeting, everyone briefly gets an arrow.
Sonar.Place.Short: Place an antenna
Sonar.PlaceCooldown: Place cooldown
Sonar.NumOfAntenna: Number of antennas
Sonar.Range: Antenna range
Sonar.ArrowDuration: Arrow duration
Sonar.ArrowAt: Arrow points to
Sonar.ArrowAt.Body: Where they died
Sonar.ArrowAt.Antenna: The antenna
Sonar.ShareBroken: Show broken antennas to everyone
Waraningyou.Name: Straw Doll
Waraningyou.Blurb: Return all the grudges at once
Waraningyou.Summary: A crewmate who stores the votes cast against them. Using "Curse" in a meeting makes your vote count as the stored votes +1.
Waraningyou.Curse: Curse
Waraningyou.Curse.Help: Use it from your own plate during a meeting (once per meeting). Your vote this meeting counts as the stored votes +1, and the store goes back to 0.
Waraningyou.Curse.Short: Spend your stored votes
Waraningyou.DefaultVote: Starting stored votes
Waraningyou.AllowSkip: Can skip in the meeting you curse
Waraningyou.Cursed: Cursed. Your vote this meeting counts as {n}
Shaman.Name: Shaman
Shaman.Blurb: Call the spirits and count your foes
Shaman.Summary: A crewmate who performs "Necromancy" in the room the arrow points to, learning at the next meeting how many living players are not crew.
Shaman.Necromancy: Necromancy
Shaman.Necromancy.Help: Stand still in the arrowed room to use it; moving interrupts it. When done, the next meeting shows how many living players are not crew. After enough tasks you also learn their role names (option).
Shaman.Necromancy.Short: Call the spirits in a room
Shaman.NecromancyCooldown: Necromancy cooldown
Shaman.NecromancyDuration: Necromancy duration
Shaman.NumOfNecromancy: Necromancy uses
Shaman.ResultViewAlivePlayers: Also show the number of living players
Shaman.SkillBoost: Get stronger with tasks
Shaman.NumOfBoostTask: Tasks needed to get stronger
Shaman.TaskCompletesRoomReroll: Completing a task picks a new room
Shaman.Done: Necromancy done. You'll learn more at the next meeting
Shaman.Interrupted: You moved, so the necromancy was interrupted
Shaman.Result: Necromancy: {n} living players are not crew
Shaman.ResultAlive: {n} players are alive
Chicken.Name: Chicken
Chicken.Blurb: A coward fears everything
Chicken.Summary: A crewmate who is scared of vents, ladders, ziplines, platforms and door panels, and may die near them at a set chance. A long blackout kills too. If alive with enough tasks done, the game end turns into a crew win (except for sabotage endings).
Chicken.WinCond: If you're alive with enough of your tasks done when the game ends, the crew wins
Chicken.VentChance: Chance to die at vents
Chicken.LadderChance: Chance to die on ladders
Chicken.ZiplineChance: Chance to die on ziplines
Chicken.PlatformChance: Chance to die on platforms
Chicken.DoorChance: Chance to die at door panels
Chicken.BlackoutTime: Die when a blackout lasts this long
Chicken.TaskPercent: Task percentage needed for the win override
ChickenMod.Name: Chicken
ChickenMod.Blurb: A coward fears everything
ChickenMod.Help: An addon that is scared of vents, ladders, ziplines, platforms and door panels, and may die near them at a set chance. A long blackout kills too.
ChickenMod.VentChance: Chance to die at vents
ChickenMod.LadderChance: Chance to die on ladders
ChickenMod.ZiplineChance: Chance to die on ziplines
ChickenMod.PlatformChance: Chance to die on platforms
ChickenMod.DoorChance: Chance to die at door panels
ChickenMod.BlackoutTime: Die when a blackout lasts this long
Prosecutor.Name: Prosecutor
Prosecutor.Blurb: Accuse and exile without a vote
Prosecutor.Summary: A crewmate who can force one player's exile in a meeting. If that player was a true crewmate, you die too (option).
Prosecutor.Prosecute: Prosecute
Prosecutor.Prosecute.Help: Use it from a player's plate during a meeting (once per meeting). The vote is redone with every vote on that player, exiling them.
Prosecutor.Prosecute.Short: Force that player's exile
Prosecutor.NumOfProsecute: Prosecute uses
Prosecutor.DieOnCrew: Die when you exile a crewmate
Prosecutor.CanCallEmergency: Can use the emergency button
Monitor.Name: Monitor
Monitor.Blurb: Be the Proxy's shadow
Monitor.Summary: The Proxy's partner madmate. You have no tasks, and you and the Proxy see each other's names in red. Your screen flashes when the Proxy kills. You win with the impostors.
Monitor.FixLights: Can fix lights
Monitor.FixComms: Can fix comms
Monitor.ImpostorVision: Impostor vision
Monitor.CanVent: Can use vents
Monitor.VentMove: Can move between vents
# ---- Roles ported from Uchu and others (impostors) ----
Proxy.Name: Proxy
Proxy.Blurb: Swap with your shadow and hide who you are
Proxy.Summary: An impostor who turns another crewmate into a Monitor (a partner madmate) at the start. You can "Swap" roles with your partner when they're nearby.
Proxy.Swap: Swap
Proxy.Swap.Help: Swaps roles with your nearby partner (Proxy ⇔ Monitor).
Proxy.Swap.Short: Swap roles with your partner
Proxy.SwapCooldown: Swap cooldown
Proxy.FollowDeath: Die together
Proxy.FollowDeath.None: Never
Proxy.FollowDeath.Proxy: Monitor dies when the Proxy dies
Proxy.FollowDeath.Monitor: Proxy dies when the Monitor dies
Proxy.FollowDeath.Either: Either dies, the other follows
EvilObserver.Name: Evil Observer
EvilObserver.Blurb: Spy on everything with hidden cameras
EvilObserver.Summary: An impostor who places cameras and watches them with "Monitor". Cameras work from the next meeting on and see through walls and blackouts.
EvilObserver.Place: Place
EvilObserver.Place.Help: Places a camera at your feet, facing your direction. It works from the next meeting on.
EvilObserver.Place.Short: Place a camera
EvilObserver.Monitor: Monitor
EvilObserver.Monitor.Help: Watches a camera. Press again to return to yourself. You can't move while watching.
EvilObserver.Monitor.Short: Watch a camera
EvilObserver.Next: Next
EvilObserver.Next.Help: Switches to another camera.
EvilObserver.Next.Short: Go to the next camera
EvilObserver.PlaceCooldown: Place cooldown
EvilObserver.NumOfCamera: Number of cameras
EvilObserver.CanSeeCameraOtherPlayer: Other players can see your cameras
EvilObserver.NoCamera: No camera is ready yet
Spectrum.Name: Spectrum
Spectrum.Blurb: Red fangs under the mask
Spectrum.BlurbWith: An impostor with the power of {role}
Spectrum.Summary: An impostor who holds one random crew role that can be a madmate. You use that role's abilities and your own kill button (no normal kill button).
Spectrum.Kill: Kill
Spectrum.Kill.Help: Kills a nearby non-impostor.
Spectrum.Kill.Short: Kill someone nearby
Spectrum.KillCooldown: Kill cooldown
Voyager.Name: Voyager
Voyager.Blurb: Hide between moments and hunt even allies
Voyager.Summary: An impostor whose "Dive" makes them invisible to non-impostors. While diving you're faster, others' looks are shuffled, and you can kill allies. If you don't "Leave" in time, you die.
Voyager.Dive: Dive
Voyager.Dive.Help: Become invisible to non-impostors and faster. Other living players' looks are swapped on your screen only. Meetings end it.
Voyager.Dive.Short: Go invisible and lurk
Voyager.AllyKill: Ally Kill
Voyager.AllyKill.Help: While diving, kills a nearby fellow impostor.
Voyager.AllyKill.Short: Kill an ally while diving
Voyager.Leave: Leave
Voyager.DiveCooldown: Dive cooldown
Voyager.DiveDuration: How long you can dive
Voyager.DiveSpeed: Speed while diving
Voyager.SwapPairs: Pairs of looks swapped
Voyager.Paradox: Paradox! You were swallowed by time
Commander.Name: Commander
Commander.Blurb: Give the order and hunt together
Commander.Summary: An impostor whose "Command" briefly shortens the kill cooldown of every impostor and madmate. Afterwards the kill cooldown is frozen for a while.
Commander.Command: Command
Commander.Command.Help: For a while, every impostor and madmate's kill cooldown becomes the set value. When it ends, impostor kill cooldowns restart and don't progress for a while.
Commander.Command.Short: Speed up everyone's kills
Commander.CommandCooldown: Command cooldown
Commander.NumOfCommand: Command uses
Commander.CommandDuration: Command duration
Commander.CommandKillCooldown: Kill cooldown during the command
Commander.KillButtonLostTime: Kill cooldown freeze after the command
Commander.Ordered: The order is given! Hunt now
Commander.Status: Command
Commander.Lost: No kills
Magician.Name: Magician
Magician.Blurb: Swap everyone's places in an instant
Magician.Summary: An impostor whose "Magic" randomly shuffles the positions of every living player.
Magician.Magic: Magic
Magician.Magic.Help: Randomly shuffles the positions of every living player. Everyone's screen flashes red, task windows close, and players in vents are pulled out.
Magician.Magic.Short: Shuffle everyone's positions
Magician.MagicCooldown: Magic cooldown
Magician.NumOfMagic: Magic uses
Kunoichi.Name: Kunoichi
Kunoichi.Blurb: Throw kunai from the shadows
Kunoichi.Summary: An impostor who throws kunai. Hitting the same player enough times kills them. Standing still lets you turn invisible.
Kunoichi.Equip: Equip
Kunoichi.Equip.Help: Takes out or puts away your kunai. While holding it you can't use the normal kill, and the kunai floats toward your mouse.
Kunoichi.Equip.Short: Take out / put away the kunai
Kunoichi.Throw: Kunai
Kunoichi.Throw.Help: Throws a kunai toward your mouse. Hitting a non-ally adds a hit, and enough hits kill them.
Kunoichi.Throw.Short: Throw a kunai
Kunoichi.Hide: Hide
Kunoichi.Hide.Help: After standing still for a while you can turn invisible. Moving ends it. Meetings end everything.
Kunoichi.Hide.Short: Stand still to go invisible
Kunoichi.ThrowCooldown: Kunai cooldown
Kunoichi.KunaiSpeed: Kunai speed
Kunoichi.WallStops: Walls stop kunai
Kunoichi.HitsToKill: Hits needed to kill
Kunoichi.FriendlyFire: Kunai can hit allies
Kunoichi.KunaiOnBody: Kunai stays on the body
Kunoichi.ResetHitsOnMeeting: Reset hits at meetings
Kunoichi.CanHide: Can hide
Kunoichi.HideWait: Time standing still before hiding
Kunoichi.HideButton: Hide with a button (otherwise automatic)
Kunoichi.ThrowWhileHidden: Can throw while hidden
SerialKiller.Name: Serial Killer
SerialKiller.Hud: Suicide in {s}s
SerialKiller.Blurb: Keep killing or die
SerialKiller.Summary: An impostor who must keep killing within a set time after their first kill, or die.
SerialKiller.Timer: Suicide Timer
SerialKiller.Timer.Help: Starts at your first kill and resets on every kill and after meetings. It stops during meetings. At 0 you die. The time left shows on the button.
SerialKiller.Timer.Short: Keep killing or die
SerialKiller.Suicide: Suicide
SerialKiller.Suicide.Help: Kill yourself (option).
SerialKiller.Suicide.Short: Kill yourself
SerialKiller.KillCooldown: Kill cooldown
SerialKiller.SuicideTime: Suicide timer
SerialKiller.SuicideButton: Has a suicide button
Warlock.Name: Warlock
Warlock.Blurb: Kill through the hands of the cursed
Warlock.Summary: An impostor with no normal kill who kills someone standing next to a cursed player, through that cursed player.
Warlock.Curse: Curse
Warlock.Curse.Help: Curses a nearby player (one at a time; they don't notice). Meetings or the cursed player's death lift the curse.
Warlock.Curse.Short: Curse someone nearby
Warlock.CurseKill: Curse Kill
Warlock.CurseKill.Help: Kills another player right next to the cursed one. The cursed player moves to where the victim was. Afterwards you're frozen and your cooldown stops for a moment.
Warlock.CurseKill.Short: Kill someone next to the cursed
Warlock.CurseCooldown: Curse cooldown
Warlock.CurseKillCooldown: Curse kill cooldown
Warlock.CanKillAllies: Can curse kill allies
Warlock.KillFreezeTime: Freeze time after a curse kill
Witch.Name: Witch
Witch.Blurb: Cast a spell and bury them after the meeting
Witch.Summary: An impostor who keeps casting a spell on a nearby player. Spelled players get a mark on their meeting plate and die at the end of the meeting if the Witch is alive.
Witch.Spell: Spell
Witch.Spell.Help: Keeps casting on a nearby player; moving away interrupts it (once per turn). Impostors can't be targeted.
Witch.Spell.Short: Cast a spell on someone nearby
Witch.SpellCooldown: Spell cooldown
Witch.SpellDuration: Spell duration
Witch.NormalKill: Can also use the normal kill
Witch.Broken: The spell was interrupted
NekoKabocha.Name: Neko Kabocha
NekoKabocha.Blurb: Take your killer with you
NekoKabocha.Summary: An impostor who takes their killer down with them. When exiled, if no other impostor is alive (or always, with the option), one player who voted for you dies too.
NekoKabocha.ExileEmbroil: Take a voter down on exile even while allies are alive
# ---- Roles ported from Uchu and others (neutral) ----
Anchor.Name: Anchor
Anchor.Blurb: Drop anchor and hold the ship
Anchor.Summary: A neutral who drops anchors at their feet. If alive at the end of a meeting after placing all of them, they win alone.
Anchor.WinCond: Win alone if you're alive at the end of a meeting after placing every anchor
Anchor.Place: Place
Anchor.Place.Help: Drops an anchor at your feet (everyone can see it; once per turn). Nearby players briefly get an arrow to it.
Anchor.Place.Short: Drop an anchor
Anchor.Echo: Echo
Anchor.Echo.Help: Opens the map; click one of your anchors to send the arrow to nearby players again from there.
Anchor.Echo.Short: Signal again from an anchor
Anchor.PlaceCooldown: Place cooldown
Anchor.NumOfAnchor: Number of anchors
Anchor.NoticeRange: Arrow range
Anchor.ArrowDuration: Arrow duration
Anchor.EchoCooldown: Echo cooldown
Anchor.NumOfEcho: Echo uses
Anchor.CanVent: Can use vents
Bettor.Name: Bettor
Bettor.Blurb: Bet on everyone's role
Bettor.Summary: A neutral who guesses everyone else's role and bets on it. Each player comes back as HIT (correct), BLOW (that role is in the game) or MISS. Get everyone HIT to win.
Bettor.WinCond: Win alone if, at the end of a meeting, you've guessed every other player's role
Bettor.Guess: Guess
Bettor.Guess.Help: Opens the guess screen to write a role for every other player. Once all are filled you can bet (once per turn; not in the first turns). HIT players' roles become visible.
Bettor.Guess.Short: Guess everyone's role and bet
Bettor.Analyze: Analyze
Bettor.Analyze.Help: Shows the team of a nearby player.
Bettor.Analyze.Short: Learn a nearby player's team
Bettor.Identify: Identify
Bettor.Identify.Help: With at least half HIT, use it from a player's plate in a meeting (once) to learn their role. Works on dead players too (option).
Bettor.Identify.Short: Learn one role in a meeting
Bettor.DisableGuessTurn: Turns you can't bet
Bettor.AnalyzeCooldown: Analyze cooldown
Bettor.NumOfAnalyze: Analyze uses
Bettor.IdentifyDead: Can identify dead players
Bettor.Title: Role Guesses
Bettor.NoGuess: (empty)
Bettor.Bet: Bet
Bettor.TooEarly: You can't bet this turn yet
Bettor.AlreadyBet: You already bet this turn
Bettor.FillAll: Fill in a guess for everyone
Bettor.RoleList: Known roles
Bettor.PickRole: What is {name}'s role?
Bettor.Back: Back
Bettor.Exists: Roles in the game
Bettor.Absent: Roles not in the game
Bettor.Result: Bet result: {hit} of {n} HIT
Bettor.Analyzed: Analyze: {name} is {team}
Bettor.Identified: Identify: {name} is {role}
Bettor.TeamImpostor: Impostor team
Bettor.TeamCrew: Crew team
Bettor.TeamNeutral: Neutral
Bettor.TeamMadmate: Impostor team
Obolus.Name: Obolus
Obolus.SealHud: Kill sealed: {n} more meetings
Obolus.Blurb: Take the ferry toll from the wicked
Obolus.Summary: A neutral with a kill button. The kill is sealed for the first few meetings. Killing an impostor (or a Jackal, option) wins alone.
Obolus.WinCond: Win alone the moment you kill an impostor (or a Jackal, option)
Obolus.Kill: Kill
Obolus.Kill.Help: Kills a nearby player (once per turn). It can't be used until the seal breaks.
Obolus.Kill.Short: Kill someone nearby
Obolus.KillCooldown: Kill cooldown
Obolus.KillShieldTurn: Meetings the kill stays sealed
Obolus.WinByJackal: Killing a Jackal also wins
Obolus.ImpostorVision: Impostor vision
Obolus.IgnoreLights: Vision isn't reduced by blackouts
Obolus.CanVent: Can use vents
Obolus.Reveal: Warn the impostors when the seal breaks
Obolus.RevealDeath: Also tell them when the Obolus dies
Obolus.Warning: Beware of the Obolus!
Obolus.Dead: The Obolus died
Seed.Name: Seed
Seed.GaugeHud: Symbiosis {a} / {b}s
Seed.Blurb: Live with someone, win with them
Seed.Summary: A neutral who wins along with whoever they "Symbiosis" with. With the gauge (option), staying near your partner fills it, and it must be full to win.
Seed.WinCond: Also win when one of your partners wins
Seed.Symbiosis: Symbiosis
Seed.Symbiosis.Help: Bonds with a nearby player. They get a ▼ only you can see, and you can see their role (option).
Seed.Symbiosis.Short: Bond with someone nearby
Seed.Gauge: Gauge
Seed.Gauge.Help: Fills while you're right next to a partner and slowly drains when you're apart. It pauses briefly after meetings.
Seed.Gauge.Short: Fills near your partner
Seed.SymbiosisCooldown: Symbiosis cooldown
Seed.NumOfSymbiosis: Symbiosis uses
Seed.SeeRole: See your partners' roles
Seed.NoWinIfPartnerDead: Can't win if the partner is dead
Seed.NoWinIfSelfDead: Can't win if you're dead
Seed.UseGauge: Use the gauge
Seed.GaugeRange: Gauge distance
Seed.GaugeNeed: Gauge needed to win
Seed.GaugeExtra: Extra gauge you can store
Seed.GaugeDecay: Drain speed when apart (per second)
Seed.PauseAfterMeeting: Gauge pause after meetings
Amnesia.Name: Amnesia
Amnesia.Blurb: Pick up the memories of the dead
Amnesia.Summary: A neutral who becomes the role of any body they report.
Amnesia.Remember: Remember
Amnesia.Remember.Help: Reporting a body turns you into that player's role at the start (or end) of the meeting. You see arrows to bodies (option).
Amnesia.Remember.Short: Become the reported body's role
Amnesia.Timing: When your role changes
Amnesia.Timing.Start: Meeting start
Amnesia.Timing.End: Meeting end
Amnesia.DeadBodyArrow: Show arrows to bodies
Amnesia.CanVent: Can use vents
Raccoon.Name: Raccoon
Raccoon.Blurb: Grab, carry and wash out the truth
Raccoon.Summary: A neutral who "Grabs" people with the kill button. A grabbed player keeps getting pulled to you. Press again to kill them, or carry them to the target room to learn their role. "Make Child" creates a Raccoon Child.
Raccoon.WinCond: When no other killers remain and the living raccoons equal the living crew, the raccoon family wins
Raccoon.Grab: Grab
Raccoon.Grab.Help: Grabs a nearby player. Press again on the grabbed player to kill them (no one else). While grabbing, a target room is shown; reaching it releases them and reveals their role. Trying to grab the parent Raccoon kills you.
Raccoon.Grab.Short: Grab / kill the grabbed
Raccoon.MakeChild: Make Child
Raccoon.MakeChild.Help: Turns a nearby player into a Raccoon Child after the next meeting (once).
Raccoon.MakeChild.Short: Make someone a Raccoon Child
Raccoon.KillCooldown: Kill cooldown
Raccoon.KillOnMeetingIfGrabbing: Kill the grabbed player when a meeting starts
Raccoon.MakeChildCooldown: Make Child cooldown
Raccoon.ChildKillCooldown: Child kill cooldown
Raccoon.ChildKillOnMeetingIfGrabbing: Children also kill the grabbed player when a meeting starts
Raccoon.Idle: Grab someone
Raccoon.GoTo: Carry them to {room}
Raccoon.Result: {name} was {role}
RaccoonChild.Name: Raccoon Child
RaccoonChild.Blurb: Grab and wash with your parent
RaccoonChild.Summary: A child made by the Raccoon. Like the Raccoon, you grab, kill and carry people to learn their roles, aiming for a win as the raccoon family.
RaccoonChild.WinCond: When no other killers remain and the living raccoons equal the living crew, the raccoon family wins
# ---- Addons ported from Uchu and others ----
Guest.Name: Guest
Guest.Blurb: Guests can't press the emergency button
Guest.Help: An addon that can't press the emergency button.
Watcher.Name: Watcher
Watcher.Blurb: No anonymous vote escapes you
Watcher.Help: An addon that sees who voted for whom even when voting is anonymous.
Invisible.Name: Invisible
Invisible.Blurb: No one can see you...
Invisible.Help: An addon that is always invisible to non-impostors. The holder doesn't know they have it (they find out when they die).
Static.Name: Static
Static.Blurb: The information is frozen
Static.Help: While it's in play, everyone's admin and vitals stay frozen as they were at the start of the game. The holder doesn't know they have it (option: they find out after dying).
Static.CanSeeAll: The holder finds out after dying
Timer.Name: Timer
Timer.Blurb: Keep the time
Timer.Help: An addon that shows the time since the last meeting under your name. It stops during meetings.
Timer.Text: Elapsed: {t}s
Visor.Name: Visor
Visor.Blurb: Watch the ship through your map
Visor.Help: An addon that shows admin whenever you open the normal map (bodies are counted too). Never given to impostors.
Visor.CanMoveWithMapWatching: Can move with the map open
Visor.CanUseAdminOnMeeting: Admin also works during meetings
Star.Name: Star
Star.Blurb: You're a star
Star.Help: An addon whose name looks yellow to everyone (rainbow with the option).
Star.RainbowStar: Rainbow
Star.RainbowSpeed: Rainbow speed
TunaMod.Name: Tuna
TunaMod.Blurb: Stop and you die
TunaMod.Help: An addon that dies when standing still. The timer pauses briefly at the start and after meetings. Seconds until death show under your name.
TunaMod.Mode: Counting
TunaMod.Mode.Usually: Continuous (time standing still in a row)
TunaMod.Mode.Total: Total (all time standing still)
TunaMod.UsuallyStop: Allowed stop time
TunaMod.TotalStop: Allowed total stop time
TunaMod.MeetingReset: Reset the total at meetings
TunaMod.MeetingStop: Timer pause after meetings
TunaMod.CountInTask: Timer runs during tasks
TunaMod.Paused: Timer paused
Moon.Name: Moon
Moon.Blurb: The moon lights up the dark
Moon.Help: An addon whose vision isn't reduced by blackouts.
Radar.Name: Radar
Radar.Blurb: Track the closest player
Radar.Help: An addon with an arrow to the closest living player.
Egoist.Name: Egoist
Egoist.Blurb: The crew's loss is my win
Egoist.Help: An addon that wins when the crew loses and loses when the crew wins (crew only). Your tasks don't count toward the crew win.
Resonance.Name: Resonance
Resonance.Blurb: Resonate with your allies' kills
Resonance.Help: An addon whose screen flashes when another impostor kills (impostors only).
Resonance.IsColorFlash: Flash in the victim's color
SpectrePossession.Name: Fox Possessed
SpectrePossession.Blurb: And now, serve that one
SpectrePossession.Help: An addon that joins the Spectre's (fox's) side (crew and impostors only). You win only when the Spectre wins, and your tasks don't count. Clairvoyance (option) lets you see through walls, and Fanaticism (option) shows the Spectre's name in the Spectre's color.
SpectrePossession.Clairvoyance: Clairvoyance (see through walls)
SpectrePossession.Fanaticism: Fanaticism (know the Spectre)
SpectrePossession.FanaticismLimit: Fanaticism needs a condition
SpectrePossession.NumOfTaskFanaticism: Tasks needed for Fanaticism (crew)
SpectrePossession.NumOfKillFanaticism: Kills needed for Fanaticism (impostor)
# ---- Ghost roles ported from Uchu ----
Baphomet.Name: Baphomet
Baphomet.Blurb: Command your familiar and steal the win
Baphomet.Summary: A ghost role for the dead of any team. Turn one living player into your familiar (Famulus) and fill your gauge by standing still next to them. If the gauge is full and your familiar is alive when the game ends, it becomes a win for you and your familiar (except for sabotage endings).
Baphomet.WinCond: With a full gauge, win with your familiar if they're alive when the game ends
Baphomet.Family: Familiar
Baphomet.Family.Help: Turns a nearby living player into your familiar (Famulus) (once). You get an arrow to them.
Baphomet.Family.Short: Make someone your familiar
Baphomet.Gauge: Gauge
Baphomet.Gauge.Help: Fills while you stand still right next to your living familiar. Standing still shows a phantom only the living can see. It drops a little at the end of meetings (not when full).
Baphomet.Gauge.Short: Stand by your familiar to fill it
Baphomet.TotalStandingTimeToWin: Gauge needed to win
Baphomet.RewindGaugeToMeetingEnd: Gauge lost at the end of meetings
Baphomet.GaugeText: Ritual
Baphomet.Cutin: The Baphomet has taken a familiar...
Famulus.Name: Famulus
Famulus.Blurb: Serve the Baphomet
Famulus.Summary: The Baphomet's familiar. You win only when the Baphomet wins, and your tasks don't count. You and the Baphomet see each other's names in purple.
Famulus.WinCond: Win only with the Baphomet
Miracle.Name: Miracle
Miracle.Blurb: Work a miracle and come back
Miracle.Summary: A ghost role for dead crewmates and impostors. Choose a living player, and at the end of the next meeting you swap roles with them.
Miracle.Swap: Swap
Miracle.Swap.Help: Choose a nearby living player. At the end of the next meeting, you and that player swap roles. Only one Miracle can choose the same player.
Miracle.Swap.Short: Swap roles with a living player
Miracle.SwapCooldown: Swap cooldown
Miracle.NumOfSwap: Swap uses
Miracle.Action: Who you can choose
Miracle.Action.MyTeam: Same team only
Miracle.Action.OtherNeutral: Anyone but neutrals
Miracle.Action.All: Anyone
